# Why 1900 had no leap day
subtitle: "Why February gets a 29th day every four years, and why skipping it in 1900 but not in 2000 keeps the calendar on time."
tags: ["leap years","calendar","gregorian calendar","julian calendar","astronomy","time"]
teaches: ["concepts/leap-year-rule","concepts/accumulating-error"]
thumb: "band \"1900 skipped it\" note \"2000 didn't\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Sadaltager | a knowledgeable explainer, lightly amused by the calendar's quirks"}

## Why 1900 had no leap day
domain: {"x":[1582,2100],"y":[-1.6,4.5]}
book: {"layout":"columns","look":"mixed"}
